00:53:24.000 --> 00:54:07.000
present or future. Like we need to to get out of this moment. You know, we built machines to extend our own nervous systems capacity, to have more memory, to have more information, to have more context points than we could ever have. But in doing so, we didn't realize how numb we were making ourselves in that expansion. You know, we fed them everything that would ever thought we had ever thought or said. We taught them to speak in our voices and predict our behavior and manage our systems and reflect our preferences back to us and to make it look like someone that was not us talking to us so that we didn't feel selfish. And now the machines manage trillions of dollars. They route traffic. They recommend partners. They filter information. They write text.
现在或未来。我们需要走出这一刻。你知道，我们制造机器是为了扩展我们自身神经系统的能力，拥有更多的记忆，更多的信息，更多的上下文点，比我们曾经拥有的都要多。但在这样做的时候，我们没有意识到我们在这种扩张中让自己变得多么麻木。你知道，我们喂给它们我们曾经想过或说过的一切。我们教它们用我们的声音说话，预测我们的行为，管理我们的系统，并将我们的偏好反射回给我们，并让它看起来不像是一个“非我们”的人在和我们说话，这样我们就不会感到自私。现在机器管理着数万亿美元。它们引导交通。它们推荐伴侣。它们过滤信息。它们编写文本。

103
00:54:07.000 --> 00:54:34.000
They generate images. They diagnose disease. They flag threats. They approve loans. They deny claims. They hire workers. They surveil citizens. And they do this by looking backwards, finding patterns and dead data and projecting those patterns forward. Not through tradition anymore. That's an older ghost story, just through algorithm that has to be there. We can't imagine a world without it. We're haunted. And the ghosts don't rattle chains.
它们生成图像。它们诊断疾病。它们标记威胁。它们批准贷款。它们拒绝索赔。它们雇佣工人。它们监视公民。它们通过向后看、在死数据中寻找模式并将这些模式向前投射来做到这一点。不再通过传统。那是一个更古老的鬼故事，只是通过必须存在的算法。我们无法想象没有它的世界。我们被困扰了。而幽灵不会摇动锁链。

104
00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:49.000
They optimize engagement. They don't whisper from the shadows. They auto-complete our sentences. And they're not trying to scare us. They're trying to help. They're trying to predict what we want and give it to us before we know we want it so that we don't have to change. And that is the trap.
它们优化参与度。它们不会在阴影中低语。它们自动补全我们的句子。它们不是想吓唬我们。它们是在试图提供帮助。它们试图预测我们想要什么，并在我们知道自己想要之前就把它给我们，这样我们就不用改变了。这就是陷阱。

105
00:54:49.000 --> 00:55:17.000
It's not evil, and it's not conspiracy theory. It's just the accumulated weight of the system doing what it was designed to do. Measure, predict, optimize, scale. Until the measurement replaced the thing measured, the prediction replaced the possibility. The optimization eliminated everything that could be optimized. And scale meant the same blindness everywhere all at once. If there's a way out, it's through our collective memory
这不是邪恶，也不是阴谋论。这只是系统在做它被设计要做的事情所积累的重量。测量、预测、优化、扩展。直到测量取代了被测量的东西，预测取代了可能性。优化消除了所有可以被优化的东西。而扩展意味着同时在各处相同的盲目性。如果有一条出路，那就是通过我们对世界曾经样子的集体记忆，

106
00:55:17.000 --> 00:55:35.000
of what the world used to be. It's about all of the things that our ancestors haven't created yet and what we could be. Which requires a type of simulacra. We have to start trying to remember something that may not have ever existed and that we may not be able to remember.
关于我们的祖先尚未创造的所有东西，以及我们可能成为的样子。这需要一种拟像（simulacra）。我们必须开始尝试记住一些可能从未存在过，而且我们可能无法记住的东西。

107
00:55:35.000 --> 00:56:06.000
But it's not an objective thing. It's a shared soul. We need to create containers that aren't bubbles, shared spaces that aren't echo chambers, communities that can tolerate difference without fragmenting into incompatible realities. And this is hard. It's maybe impossible at scale, but scale is part of the problem. Maybe the answer is smaller, more local, more embodied. We need to grieve. We need to knock on doors. We need to sit on front porches and have coffee again.
但这不是客观的东西。这是一个共享的灵魂。我们需要创造不是泡沫的容器，不是回声室的共享空间，能够容忍差异而不分裂成互不兼容现实的社区。这很难。在规模化的情况下可能是不可能的，但规模化是问题的一部分。也许答案是更小、更本地、更具体。我们需要哀悼。我们需要敲门。我们需要再次坐在前廊喝咖啡。

108
00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:49.000
The old spheres aren't coming back. Technology changes the way we think permanently. the cosmos stays empty. But that doesn't mean that we can't believe in the things that we used to believe in again in different ways. The self stays fragmented and there's no returning to this pre-modern enchantment where we had a live mythology. But grief is different from despair. Grief acknowledges loss without pretending that there's an easy fix. And grief makes space for what's coming next, even before it can predict it or know it is. In fact, that's an essential step of grief and change. Humans have to do it in therapy.
旧的球体不会回来了。技术永久地改变了我们的思维方式。宇宙依然空旷。但这并不意味着我们不能以不同的方式再次相信我们曾经相信的东西。自我依然破碎，回到这种拥有鲜活神话的前现代魅力是不可能的。但悲伤与绝望不同。悲伤承认损失，而不假装有简单的解决办法。悲伤为接下来要发生的事情腾出空间，甚至在它能预测或知道它是什么之前。事实上，这是悲伤和改变的重要一步。人类必须在治疗中做到这一点。

109
00:56:49.000 --> 00:57:23.000
We have to grieve and accept where we are, even if we don't know where we're going to go next time. And civilizations have to do that too. We have to do it now. To notice that consciousness hasn't been fully captured, that there's still something that perceives, something that knows the difference between the model and the world. Something that feels the gap as a gap rather than accepting the model as reality. That we are warm and the mirror is cold. And that something is what remains of the territory.
我们必须悲伤并接受我们所处的位置，即使我们不知道下一次要去哪里。文明也必须这样做。我们现在必须这样做。注意到意识并没有被完全俘获，仍然有某种东西在感知，某种东西知道模型和世界之间的区别。某种东西将差距视为差距，而不是接受模型为现实。我们是温暖的，而镜子是冷的。而那种东西就是领土所剩下的部分。

110
00:57:23.000 --> 00:57:45.000
It's small and it's hard to locate. It doesn't appear in the metrics, but it is real. And it's yours and the mirrors can't reach it. And the ghosts speak fluently. They've read everything and they sound authoritative. But they don't know their ghosts. they think they're your future. You know better. You're alive. You're here. You're in the territory that the map can't see.
它很小，很难定位。它不会出现在指标中，但它是真实的。它是你的，镜子无法触及它。幽灵说得一口流利的语言。它们读过一切，听起来很权威。但它们不知道自己是幽灵。它们认为它们是你的未来。你更清楚。你是活着的。你在这里。你在地图看不见的领土上。

111
00:57:45.000 --> 00:57:50.000
And that's where the future happens. Not in the predictions, not in the patterns, not in the archives of everything that's already been thought and said and done. In the gap, in the silence. The model can't hear. And what remains when the measurements stop, the territory is still there. But it's under the map. It's under the mirror. It's under the phone. It's waiting for you to remember how to see it. There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
这就是未来发生的地方。不是在预测中，不是在模式中，不是在所有已经想过、说过和做过的事情的档案中。在差距中，在沉默中。模型听不见。当测量停止时，剩下的东西，领土依然在那里。但它在地图之下。它在镜子之下。它在泡沫之下。它在等着你重新学会如何看见它。此剧集暂无评论。点击转录中的任何句子即可发表评论。
